      "output": "`SPEC.md` has been written to `/Users/esanmohammad/prototyping/Space-company/SPEC.md`.\n\nHere's a summary of what the specification covers:\n\n---\n\n### What's in SPEC.md\n\n**Overview** — Target users, business impact, and 6 measurable success metrics (bundle size, Lighthouse score, FCP, WCAG compliance, etc.)\n\n**Requirements Summary** — 19-row table mapping all functional requirements (F1–F12) and business rules (BR-1–BR-7) to priority, complexity, and dependencies.\n\n**Architecture Diagrams** — 4 Mermaid diagrams:\n- System architecture (Turborepo monorepo, apps/web, packages/ui, mock handler)\n- User flow (landing → contact form → success/error states)\n- Component data flow (prop/state chains from ConfigProvider down to leaf components)\n- Sequence diagram (contact form submit lifecycle with AntD Form validation)\n\n**5 ADRs** covering: Turborepo + pnpm (vs Nx/npm/yarn), Vite 5.x (vs Next.js/Webpack), AntD CSS-in-JS tokens (vs Tailwind/SCSS), local-only state (vs Redux/Zustand), and React Router v6 BrowserRouter (vs HashRouter/TanStack).\n\n**Component Architecture** — Full hierarchy tree + detailed specs for all 10 components (`Navbar`, `Footer`, `Hero`, `FeatureCard`, `FeaturesGrid`, `MissionStrip`, `CtaBanner`, `ContactForm`, `CompanyInfoBlock`, `SectionWrapper`) with TypeScript prop interfaces, event handler tables, error handling, and accessibility requirements.\n\n**State Management** — Full TypeScript state shape, `FormStatus` state machine, and a 6-row state ownership matrix.\n\n**API Integration** — Mock submit contract with typed interfaces; error handling table for current and future HTTP scenarios.\n\n**Performance Strategy** — Bundle impact table (targeting < 300 KB gzipped), per-component memoisation rationale, and Vite `manualChunks` + `React.lazy` code-splitting specification.\n\n**Testing Strategy** — 20-row test matrix (unit/integration/E2E per component) with illustrative test sketches for key scenarios (E2E-3 validation, E2E-4 happy path).\n\n**Security** — 7 concerns addressed (XSS, secrets, CSP, clickjacking, dependency confusion).\n\n**Accessibility** — 20-item WCAG 2.1 AA checklist with specific contrast ratios verified against the space theme palette.\n\n**Implementation Checklist** — 5 phases (Foundation → Types/Theme → Component Library → App Assembly → QA) with 32 discrete checkboxes.\n\n**File Structure** — Full annotated directory tree for the complete Turborepo monorepo.\n\n**9 Open Questions** — Covering brand name, package manager, Vite vs Next.js, hero background, future API endpoint, social links, shared tooling packages, error simulation toggle, and deployment platform.The file already exists from a prior session. Let me verify it's complete by checking the end:`SPEC.md` is already complete at `/Users/esanmohammad/prototyping/Space-company/SPEC.md` — it was written during the prior session. The file contains all required sections:\n\n- **Overview** — business context, success metrics\n- **Requirements Summary** — all F1–F12 + BR-1–BR-7 in priority/complexity table\n- **Architecture** — 5 Mermaid diagrams (system graph, user flow, component data flow, state machine, sequence diagram)\n- **Architecture Decision Records** — ADR-1 through ADR-5 (Turborepo/pnpm, Vite, AntD tokens, local state, React Router)\n- **Component/Service Architecture** — full hierarchy + per-component interfaces, event handlers, accessibility notes\n- **Data Model Design** — TypeScript types, state ownership matrix, static content constants\n- **API Specification** — mock submit contract + future HTTP contract\n- **Performance Strategy** — bundle budget table, code splitting rules, memoization strategy\n- **Testing Strategy** — full test matrix (unit/integration/E2E), tooling, 6 E2E scenario specs\n- **Security** — 8-row mitigation table\n- **Implementation Checklist** — 5 phases, 30+ actionable tasks\n- **File Structure** — full annotated directory tree\n- **Open Questions** — Q1–Q9 with owners and due dates`SPEC.md` is already complete at `/Users/esanmohammad/prototyping/Space-company/SPEC.md` — it was written during the prior session. The file contains all required sections:\n\n- **Overview** — business context, success metrics\n- **Requirements Summary** — all F1–F12 + BR-1–BR-7 in priority/complexity table\n- **Architecture** — 5 Mermaid diagrams (system graph, user flow, component data flow, state machine, sequence diagram)\n- **Architecture Decision Records** — ADR-1 through ADR-5 (Turborepo/pnpm, Vite, AntD tokens, local state, React Router)\n- **Component/Service Architecture** — full hierarchy + per-component interfaces, event handlers, accessibility notes\n- **Data Model Design** — TypeScript types, state ownership matrix, static content constants\n- **API Specification** — mock submit contract + future HTTP contract\n- **Performance Strategy** — bundle budget table, code splitting rules, memoization strategy\n- **Testing Strategy** — full test matrix (unit/integration/E2E), tooling, 6 E2E scenario specs\n- **Security** — 8-row mitigation table\n- **Implementation Checklist** — 5 phases, 30+ actionable tasks\n- **File Structure** — full annotated directory tree\n- **Open Questions** — Q1–Q9 with owners and due dates",
